  "methods": "Retain the six calibration/five evaluation fly partition, all 65 observed repeats, both correction scenarios and all four fixed passive circuits. Both candidates have fast inactivation. Shared kinetics dz/dt=(m-z)/tau is nested in separate kinetics dz/dt=m*(1-z)/tau_on-(1-m)*z/tau_off. Shared tau bounds remain 0.05-3s; separate on 0.01-3s and off 0.05-3s. All other parameter bounds remain as in the full-pulse experiment. Refit both candidates under the same phase-scaled objective, giving equal weight to each calibration cell and phase after division by fixed calibration-only phase scales. Scale is the RMS of the six observed cell-mean waveforms in that phase, floored at 1mV; it is an amplitude normalization, not an estimated noise model. Two fixed starts, log-parameter optimization, max100 evaluations per start. No measured post-pulse state is supplied. Always observe model voltage at original 10kHz sample times even when refining the solver; average ten samples identically to data. Repeat history is explicitly propagated to a second pulse at 60s onset interval. Scores retain physical mV units and normalized phase errors. All source waveforms have previously been seen: retrospective conditional transfer only.",
